# Build outputs.  Per RELEASE, not per repo: each of v8/, v9/, v10/ builds its
# own world, and two of them cannot share a rootfs.
build/
rootfs/

# THE EXTENSION RULES ARE GONE, AND THEY WERE DELETING BELL LABS' SOURCE.
#
# This list used to carry `*.o', `*.a', `*.i' and `*.out' for build outputs.
# They match by extension ANYWHERE, including inside third_party/, which is
# supposed to be the pristine vendored archive the whole fidelity claim rests
# on -- and every build output this project makes already lands under build/
# or rootfs/, both ignored wholesale above.  Measured: dropping all four makes
# 346 files trackable and NOT ONE of them is a build product.
#
# What they had been deleting:
#
#   * TEN `.c.a' SOURCE BUNDLES.  usr/src/libplot stores each library's C
#     files inside an ar archive and the makefile runs `ar x' to get at them,
#     so these are the only copy of that source.  `git log --all -- *.c.a' was
#     empty: never tracked once.  On a fresh clone tools/import.sh could not
#     have imported any plot library at all.
#
#   * FOUR TEST SUITES WRITTEN BY THE PROGRAMS' OWN AUTHORS, already imported
#     into src/ and silently dropped -- eqn/eqntest.a (37 cases), tbl/samples.a
#     (54), pic/pictest.a (36), hoc/tests.a (10).  137 acceptance tests, in the
#     tree, uncommitted and unrun, while this port tested those programs
#     against cases it wrote itself.
#
#   * The shipped libraries and font tables in third_party/, which several
#     recorded measurements cite -- "V8's libm.a is 216 bytes, one member whose
#     whole symbol table is a row of underscores" is not reproducible from a
#     clone without them.
#
# It could only ever fail on CI: the files are present locally, so the build,
# all seventeen suites and a 7579-invocation crash probe passed here against
# source that did not exist in the repository.  A runner is the only machine
# with no history -- the same reason the /etc/utmp case in tests/jail could
# only fail there.
#
# tools/import.sh now runs `git check-ignore --no-index' on every destination
# and warns, so the next one speaks at the point of the mistake.

# Scratch at the REPO ROOT, which is where debugging lands when a reproduction
# is quicker to write than to place.  313 KB of it got committed -- fourteen
# files including four Mach-O binaries (gw, ls1, pwd2, so) -- because the list
# above covers *.o and *.out and nothing else these produce.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: compiler/crt0.s, compiler/setjmp.s and
# shim/v8sys/sigtramp.s are real tracked sources and must stay tracked.
/*.s
/*.c
/*.h
#
# An EXTENSIONLESS binary cannot be pattern-matched apart from a legitimate
# file, so this list cannot be complete and is not the guard.  tests/deps
# asserts the root holds nothing but the known files -- see the case there.

# Stage-0 host-built tools
/tools/bin/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Xcode (Phase 5)
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
